      "question": "A reference frame 'a' rotates with respect to another reference frame 'b' with an angular velocity w. If the position, velocity and acceleration of a particle in reference frame 'a' are represented by r, va, aa then show that acceleration in frame 'b' is given by ab = aa + 2(w × va) + w × (w × r) + (dw/dt) × r. Explain the physical significance of various terms in the above expression and show that Coriolis force and centrifugal forces are consequence of rotation of the frame of reference.",
